<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>Top Rental Tips | RideWave</title>

    <link rel="stylesheet"
        href="https://unpkg.com/boxicons@2.1.4/css/boxicons.min.css">

    <style>

        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #f7f8fc;
            color: #08123B;
        }

        /* =========================
           NAVBAR
        ========================= */

        .navbar {
            height: 90px;
            background: #ffffff;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: space-between;
            padding: 0 7%;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.06);
        }

        .logo img {
            height: 90px;
            width: auto;
            display: block;
            object-fit: contain;
        }

        .nav-links {
            display: flex;
            gap: 30px;
        }

        .nav-links a {
            text-decoration: none;
            color: #08123B;
            font-weight: 600;
            transition: .3s;
        }

        .nav-links a:hover {
            color: #FF532E;
        }

        /* =========================
           HERO
        ========================= */

        .blog-hero {
            background: #08123B;
            padding: 80px 20px;
            text-align: center;
            color: white;
        }

        .blog-hero span {
            color: #FF532E;
            font-weight: 600;
            font-size: 15px;
        }

        .blog-hero h1 {
            font-size: 48px;
            margin-top: 15px;
        }

        /* =========================
           BLOG CONTENT
        ========================= */

        .blog-container {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 60px auto;
            padding: 0 25px;
        }

        .blog-image {
            width: 100%;
            max-height: 480px;
            object-fit: cover;
            border-radius: 18px;
            margin-bottom: 40px;
        }

        .blog-content h2 {
            font-size: 30px;
            margin: 35px 0 15px;
        }

        .blog-content p {
            font-size: 17px;
            line-height: 1.9;
            color: #555;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        .blog-content ul {
            margin: 20px 0 30px 25px;
        }

        .blog-content li {
            margin-bottom: 12px;
            color: #555;
            line-height: 1.7;
        }

        /* =========================
           BACK BUTTON
        ========================= */

        .back-btn {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 8px;
            margin-top: 25px;
            padding: 13px 22px;
            background: #FF532E;
            color: white;
            text-decoration: none;
            border-radius: 8px;
            font-weight: 600;
            transition: .3s;
        }

        .back-btn:hover {
            transform: translateY(-3px);
            background: #e94320;
        }

        /* =========================
           FOOTER
        ========================= */

        footer {
            background: #08123B;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 30px 20px;
            margin-top: 70px;
        }

        footer p {
            color: #ccc;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }

        footer a {
            color: white;
            text-decoration: none;
            margin: 0 10px;
        }

        footer a:hover {
            color: #FF532E;
        }

        @media(max-width: 768px) {

            .navbar {
                padding: 0 20px;
            }

            .nav-links {
                display: none;
            }

            .blog-hero h1 {
                font-size: 34px;
            }

            .blog-container {
                margin: 40px auto;
            }

        }

    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <!-- NAVBAR -->

    <nav class="navbar">

        <a href="/" class="logo">
            <img src="/images/logo.png" alt="RideWave">
        </a>

        <div class="nav-links">
            <a href="/">Home</a>
            <a href="/#rentals">Rentals</a>
            <a href="/teams">Teams</a>
            <a href="/#faq">FAQ</a>
            <a href="/blog">Clips</a>
            <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
        </div>

    </nav>


    <!-- HERO -->

    <section class="blog-hero">

        <span>15 May 2026</span>

        <h1>
            Top Rental Tips for 2026
        </h1>

    </section>


    <!-- CONTENT -->

    <main class="blog-container">

        <img
            src="/images/blog-1.jpg"
            alt="Car Rental Tips"
            class="blog-image"
        >

        <div class="blog-content">

            <p>
                Renting a car can make your journey more comfortable,
                flexible, and convenient. However, choosing the wrong
                rental option can increase your travel expenses.
            </p>

            <h2>1. Compare Rental Prices</h2>

            <p>
                Before booking a vehicle, compare prices between
                different rental options. Look beyond the basic daily
                price and check additional charges, deposits, taxes,
                and insurance costs.
            </p>

            <h2>2. Choose the Right Vehicle</h2>

            <p>
                Select a vehicle according to your journey. A compact
                car may be perfect for city travel, while an SUV can
                provide more comfort and luggage space for long trips.
            </p>

            <h2>3. Check the Rental Terms</h2>

            <p>
                Always read the rental terms before confirming your
                booking. Pay attention to fuel policies, mileage
                limits, cancellation rules, security deposits, and
                late-return charges.
            </p>

            <h2>4. Inspect the Car</h2>

            <p>
                Check the vehicle carefully before starting your trip.
                Look for scratches, dents, tyre condition, lights,
                mirrors, and other visible damage.
            </p>

            <h2>5. Book in Advance</h2>

            <p>
                Booking your rental car early can give you more vehicle
                choices and potentially better prices, especially
                during holidays and busy travel seasons.
            </p>

            <h2>Final Tip</h2>

            <p>
                A good rental experience starts with choosing the right
                vehicle and understanding the rental agreement.
                Take a few minutes to compare your options before
                making a booking.
            </p>

            <a href="/blog" class="back-btn">
                <i class="bx bx-left-arrow-alt"></i>
                Back to Clips
            </a>

        </div>

    </main>


    <!-- FOOTER -->

    <footer>

        <p>
            © 2026 RideWave. All Rights Reserved.
        </p>

        <div>
            <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
            <a href="/refunds">Refunds Policy</a>
            <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>
        </div>

    </footer>

</body>
</html>